From a15f8a8cc0d4806a539e3177e06fc6de7ed9e47e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 19:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: wire AXP318W PMIC IRQ via the NMI/R-INTC

The AXP8191/AXP318W PMIC (`clk-sunxi-ng-a733-r-ccu-add-r-i2c0-gate-reset`, HW-proven at r_i2c0 0-0036) was
described without an interrupt, so the mfd core runs it with no IRQ --
no power-key events, no regulator/thermal/battery interrupts, only
polled access. Add its interrupt path through the A733 NMI (R-INTC)
controller.

The NMI controller is three registers in the PRCM at 0x07010000:
NMI_INT_CTRL 0x0320, NMI_INT_EN 0x0324, NMI_INT_PEND 0x0328, i.e. a 0xc window at 0x07010320 -- the
same reg the A523 NMI node uses, register-for-register. Its GIC line,
however, is A733-specific: the A733 user manual lists source
"NMI" at intid 220 -> gic_spi 188 (vector 0x0370). The A523 dtsi uses
GIC_SPI 148; that value is REJECTED here -- copying it blindly is the
exact a523-derived error that already produced a wrong r_i2c0 base and
IRQ on this track. USE 188, verified against the interrupt list of the A733 user manual.

Because the register layout is identical to the A523 NMI, the in-tree
sun55i-a523-nmi irqchip driver (CONFIG_SUNXI_NMI_INTC) is reused via a
fallback compatible "allwinner,sun60i-a733-nmi","allwinner,sun55i-a523-nmi",
the same pattern the r_pio node uses for the r-pinctrl.

The AXP IRQ pin is active-low and wired to NMI input line 0, so the
pmic@36 node gets interrupt-parent = <&nmi_intc> / interrupts =
<0 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>. The PMIC is itself the irq controller for its
sub-devices, hence interrupt-controller / #interrupt-cells = <1>,
matching the mainline axp examples and the sun55i-a523 avaota axp717
node.

Compile-verified: dtb builds with 0 warnings and decompiles with the
nmi_intc node (interrupts GIC_SPI 188) and the pmic@36
interrupt-parent/interrupts present; the sun55i-a523-nmi irqchip object
compiles with CONFIG_SUNXI_NMI_INTC=y.
HW-PENDING: actual IRQ delivery is unproven -- it needs a PMIC event
stimulus (power-key press / IRQ-status change) on a live board.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
 .../sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts         | 37 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
index 412164a..a95f325 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -1565,6 +1565,28 @@ r_ccu: clock-controller@7010000 {
 			#reset-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * NMI / R-INTC. Three registers in the PRCM (0x07010000):
+		 * NMI_INT_CTRL 0x0320, NMI_INT_EN 0x0324, NMI_INT_PEND 0x0328
+		 * -- so the controller window is
+		 * 0x07010320 + 0xc. Its GIC line is the A733 "NMI" interrupt:
+		 * per the UM interrupt list, intid 220 -> gic_spi 188
+		 * (vector 0x0370). This is NOT the A523's GIC_SPI 148 -- that
+		 * number is wrong for this silicon, and is exactly the class of
+		 * a523-copy error that already bit the r_i2c0 base/IRQ on this
+		 * track. Register layout is identical to the A523 NMI, so the
+		 * in-tree sun55i-a523-nmi driver is reused via the fallback
+		 * compatible (same pattern as the r_pio node below).
+		 */
+		nmi_intc: interrupt-controller@7010320 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-nmi",
+				     "allwinner,sun55i-a523-nmi";
+			reg = <0x0 0x07010320 0x0 0xc>;
+			interrupt-controller;
+			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 188 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		};
+
 		r_pio: pinctrl@7025000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-r-pinctrl",
 				     "allwinner,sun55i-a523-r-pinctrl";
@@ -1619,6 +1641,21 @@ pmic@36 {
 				compatible = "x-powers,axp318w";
 				reg = <0x36>;
 
+				/*
+				 * AXP IRQ pin is active-low and feeds the NMI
+				 * input, line 0. The PMIC is itself the irq
+				 * controller for its sub-devices (power key,
+				 * regulators), so #interrupt-cells = <1> (matches
+				 * the mainline axp examples / the sun55i-a523
+				 * avaota axp717 node). HW-PENDING: the actual IRQ
+				 * delivery still needs a PMIC event stimulus on a
+				 * board to be proven.
+				 */
+				interrupt-parent = <&nmi_intc>;
+				interrupts = <0 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+				interrupt-controller;
+				#interrupt-cells = <1>;
+
 				regulators {
 					/*
 					 * SWOUT1 = reg 0x11 BIT(3) = Maxio PHY
-- 
